## 2. Compressor

Keep Moh's order reversal explicit:

\[
 \widehat T_i(F,G)=T_i^\psi(G,F),\qquad
 B_i={\partial\widehat T_i\over\partial G},\qquad
 J(F,\widehat T_i)=B_iJ(F,G).                    \tag{2.1}
\]

For the two degree pairs the exact characteristic data are

\[
 (M,d,D)=((-66,77,97),(99,33,11,1),(66,55,145))
\]

and

\[
 (M,d,D)=((-72,81,106),(108,36,9,1),(72,63,227)).
\]

The complete constant-target second characteristic family is

\[
 \widehat T_2=G^3-F^2+aG^2+bFG+cF+dG+e_0,
 \qquad B_2=3G^2+2aG+bF+d.
\]

Its leading \(3G^2\) cannot cancel, so \(\deg B_2=2m\). Total-degree
attainment and (2.1) give, for \(j\ne0\),

\[
 \deg j\le n+D_2-2-2m=20\quad\hbox{or}\quad25.
\]

At \(T_3\), Proposition 3.2 gives
\(\deg_yB_3=D_3+M_3=242\) or 333, exactly the upper bound
\(n+D_3-2\) for \(\deg J(F,\widehat T_3)\). Domain degree additivity
therefore forces \(\deg j=0\) when \(j\ne0\). Theorem B, whose proof uses
the actual source faces and attained \(T_2\), excludes \(j=0\). In
particular, \(T_2\) alone supplies only the 20/25 bound; both attained levels
and the source theorem are needed for the compressor.

## 3. Complete targets and source support

Put \(x=t^{-1}\), \(y=(1+z)t^{-1}\); \(t,z\) are extraction symbols and
are not solver variables. For \(k=33\) or 36, define

\[
 H_0=h-\frac b6t^k,
 \quad v=D+\left(\frac a3+\frac{b^2}{18}\right)t^{2k-1},
\]

\[
 V=C-\frac b4t^kD+
 \left(\frac{ab}{12}+\frac{b^3}{54}-\frac c2\right)t^{3k-1},
 \qquad U={8V\over3t}.
\]

Let \(R\) be the part of \(v^2-UH_0\) below \(z\)-degree \(k\); every
high-\(z\) coefficient is a row. With
\(p=d+bc/2-(a+b^2/4)^2/3\), the exact shortened expression is

\[
 Q_*={3\over4}RH_0^2-{1\over8}tvUH_0+tvR-{9\over64}t^2U^2
 +pt^{4k-2}H_0^2+pt^{4k-1}v+qt^{6k-2}.          \tag{3.1}
\]

The \(6k-2\) \(H\)-adic normalizer puts the \(T_2\) faces at depths 141
and 151. They are the physical 143 and 153 rows after the proved two-unit
denominator shedding. That shift is bookkeeping, not a gauge action.

Every strict-below row has target zero. Every equality row subtracts the
entire target:

\[
 T_2:\quad \lambda_2z^{40}(1+z)^{15}\ (99),\qquad
 \lambda_2z^{49}(1+z)^{14}\ (108),
\]

over all 56 or 64 slots, including zero slots, and

\[
 T_3:\quad \lambda_3z^{105}(1+z)^{40}\ (99),\qquad
 \lambda_3z^{176}(1+z)^{51}\ (108),
\]

over all 146 or 228 slots. Separate rows
\(Z_2\lambda_2-1\) and \(Z_3\lambda_3-1\) keep both leaders free and
nonzero; neither leader is set to one.

The active recurrences are

\[
 T_3=T_2^3-\lambda_2^3FG+u_{11}t^{11}FT_2\pmod {t^{21}}, \tag{3.2}
\]

including `t3eq+leader55^3`, and

\[
 T_3=T_2^4-\lambda_2^4FG^2+u_9t^9FGT_2
       +u_{18}t^{18}FT_2^2\pmod {t^{26}},       \tag{3.3}
\]

including `t3eq+leader63^4`. Seven later 99 coefficients and thirteen later
D108 coefficients are omitted only as proved passive polynomial extensions,
never set to zero.

For both 99 charts, the two-point/split and source-support equations are
already composed into the frozen semantic parametrization, leaving zero
residual source rows. D108 instead retains and emits its 14 residual rows.

| chart | base face \(P\) | complete source-support contract |
