At-level source rows subtract those whole targets; strictly lower rows have
zero target. The D108 chart retains free `minor_mean` \(\mu\), does not split
the quadratic or choose a root, and retains all 14 source residuals.

## 4. Gauge ledger

The ledger is explicit. `beta=1` spends simultaneous dilation exactly once,
via \(F_\alpha=\alpha^{-n}F(\alpha x,\alpha y)\) and
\(G_\alpha=\alpha^{-m}G(\alpha x,\alpha y)\). On the 99 charts, the
audited diagonal translation licenses `jet0=0`; the omitted coordinate is a
free affine-line factor. D108 instead uses the repaired free-mean chart and
retains `minor_mean`; no inherited mean-zero slice is substituted.

The separation parameter \(\rho\) or \(c\) is free and only inverted by an
explicit equation. The characteristic leaders remain free nonzero scalars.
The Jacobian scalar is not normalized; its omission is a consequence of § 2.
The 141/143 and 151/153 conversion is denominator shedding. No root choice,
split variable, leader normalization, separation normalization, or hidden
centering spends another gauge.

## 5. Direct presentation and substitution proof

Let \(A=\mathbb Q[s_1,\ldots,s_m]\) be the semantic ring and
\(B=A[X_1,\ldots,X_N]\). The circuit rows are

\[
 d_i=X_i-f_i(s,X_1,\ldots,X_{i-1}),              \tag{5.1}
\]

each monic with coefficient +1 and ordered acyclically. Recursive evaluation
defines \(\phi:B\to A\). Successive monic division has a unique remainder in
\(A\), hence

\[
 \ker\phi=(d_1,\ldots,d_N),\qquad
 {B\over(d,c_1,\ldots,c_r)}\simeq
 {A\over(\phi(c_1),\ldots,\phi(c_r))}.           \tag{5.2}
\]

This is ideal equivalence, not merely equality of zero sets; it uses no
division and has no vanished-leader branch. The frozen production audit had
already checked every one of the 7,136/17,308 definitions for leader +1,
preceding dependencies, and exact round trip. The direct builder evaluates
the same graph in the frozen semantic coordinate ring and emits only
primitive integral images of constraint rows.

The exact-\(\mathbb Q\) control used three graph leaders `u,v,w`, checked both
ideal containments and the semantic elimination ideal, and rejected a one-unit
