## 8. FALLACY-v2 acceptance audit

- Modular unit is only a signal; exact replay on identical generators or an
  exact cofactor is required for a kill.
- Subideal unit implies full-ideal unit. Subideal nonunit implies nothing
  about full-ideal properness.
- A complete exact-Q nonunit result would require dimension and a sample point
  before the loud necessary-survivor type above.
- A necessary-chart survivor is not a pair and not a canonical lift.
- Flag, physical place, and cover series remain distinct. No exit price or
  first-separation count is asserted.
- Strict-below zero rows and at-level coefficient-minus-complete-target rows
  are separate. Proposition 2.2/Theorem A supplies attainment; Proposition
  4.6 supplies the complete \(T_3\) face. No floor is called equality.
- Source map, coefficient field, semantic and solver order, alias map, and
  generator hashes are declared. Matching names are not a ring map.
- No `sat()` wrapper, raw remainder heuristic, root selection, or
  vanished-leader division is used.
- Prime marks are labels unless an explicit derivative is written.
- Fixed characteristic indices are not conflated with arrival/search labels.
- No pole/interior, carrier, family-C child, or canonical-lift claim is filled
  by analogy.

No new exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis=` line is applicable.

