+| Frozen report’s “proper complete direct ideal … not a Keller pair” | REFUTED | No exhibited pair or canonical lift is a different statement |
+
+The corrected mathematical claims and subset implication are promotable. The unchanged full executable and the frozen report as a whole are not. This gate neither changes a ledger nor declares a production unit.
+
+**Custody.** Before any write, `df -h /` reported 96G total, 85G used, 12G available. I built the nine-entry manifest with `awk` from the indexed basename/SHA fields of `xmodel/t2t3-compressor-gate-astra-20260906.run.v2`, then ran `sha256sum -c`. All nine frozen files under `/tmp/jc2-lane.BkloGL/inputs` returned `OK`. The manifest and mechanical output are retained in [gate notes](/home/ubuntu/jc2/box/t2t3-compressor-gate-20260906/charged-check.txt). Frozen receipt basis: `36db4240df0b96565569a65780af015292051537`.
+
+All citations to charged basenames below mean those verified frozen copies. Supplementary source maps were checked against the exact hashes embedded in `build_direct.py:35–83`; the graph producer was checked against its retained custody SHA `bc83ab1560f418038c7cc26cca003c45fb51ac8745ef2ae4cb5d257438ba6ca4`. No `ideation-*` input, `jc2-lean`, charged-input mutation, or ledger edit was used.
+
+**The compressor, re-derived.** Keep physical coordinates separate from Moh’s formal target variables: `(f,g)=(G,F)`, with `deg F=deg_y F=n`, `deg G=deg_y G=m`. Write `Q=T₂^ψ(G,F)`, `W=T₃^ψ(G,F)`, and `B_i=(∂T_i^ψ/∂f)(G,F)`. Then
+
+\[
+J(F,Q)=B_2J(F,G),\qquad J(F,W)=B_3J(F,G).
+\]
+
+The derivative is with respect to the formal first argument before composition; it is not a physical derivative or an ambiguous prime label. Moh p.150’s definitions give the following exact arithmetic, also recomputed in `arithmetic-check.json`:
+
+| `(n,m)` | `M` | `d` | `Λ` | characteristic degrees `D` |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `(99,66)` | `−66,77,97` | `99,33,11,1` | `−6534,−1815,−1595` | `66,55,145` |
+| `(108,72)` | `−72,81,106` | `108,36,9,1` | `−7776,−2268,−2043` | `72,63,227` |
+
+Lemma 2.1, p.151, uses Keller to obtain `e=n−1` and constant earlier series coefficients. Proposition 2.1, p.152, commutes approximate-root formation with coefficient specialization `ψ:x→0`. This specializes the target coefficients; it does not evaluate the physical source coordinate after composition. Proposition 2.2, pp.152–154, gives **exact y-degree** `D_i`, and a nonzero scalar leader for `M_i<e`. Here `97<98` and `106<107`; neither index is the exceptional terminal `M_i=e`. Moh explicitly says on p.154 that monic means unit leader, not a coefficient normalized to one.
+
+The requested pp.150–157 are insufficient for the complete argument. Proposition 3.1 is on p.157, with specialization on p.159; Proposition 3.2 is on pp.159–161. More importantly, Proposition 2.2 alone does not establish total degree. The needed necessity argument is the proof of Proposition 4.5 on p.172, under `M₃=n−2` and the Keller setup. Its minimum ranges over roots of `g∏_{i≤3}T_i^ψ`, including T₃, and excludes order below −1. Scalar leading coefficient and root orders at least −1 give `deg_x[y^{D−j}]T_i≤j`, hence total degree `D_i`. Thus the total-degree blocks are justified for the actual Keller realizations; this argument must not be used backwards to assume Keller for arbitrary chart points. See frozen `char-degree-instrument…:28–40,53–79` and the verified Moh PDF, printed pp.169–172.
+
+Proposition 3.1 enumerates exactly
+
+\[
+Q=G^3-F^2+aG^2+bFG+cF+dG+e_0,
+\quad B_2=3G^2+2aG+bF+d.
