+The coefficient of `F²` is −1 because it is the unique equality-weight cancellation against the monic `G³`. All five lower coefficients remain free. Since `2m>n,m`, `3G²` is the unique highest-degree term in `B₂`, so `deg B₂=2m`. If `j=J(F,G)≠0` and `deg Q=D₂`, degree additivity in the polynomial domain gives
