+There is a noncircular check for the retained existential recurrence as well. At 99, its active representative is `W=Q³−λ₂³FG+uFQ`. The derivative’s term `3Q²B₂` has degree 242; other active derivatives have degree at most 231. All seven passive correction monomials have total degree at most 132, below 145. At 108, use `W=Q⁴−λ₂⁴FG²+uFGQ+vFQ²`; `4Q³B₂` has degree 333, and all other active derivatives have degree at most 324. The thirteen passive monomials have degree at most 216, below 227. These statements follow by enumerating `nj+ma+D₂b≤n₂D₂`, `a<3`, `b<n₂`. Thus actual total-degree attainment and the displayed recursive support already prove the derivative assertion; canonicality is sufficient but is not required for this elementary implication.
+
+**Which Theorem B, and its zero case.** The relevant theorem is the one stated in frozen `char-degree-instrument…:120–132`. It is a campaign theorem about actual source faces, not a theorem labelled B in Moh. A source-support closeout whose premise is a nonzero monomial Jacobian cannot establish the missing `j≠0` premise.
+
+Suppose `j=0`. In characteristic zero, the common-polynomial theorem gives `F=f(H),G=g(H)`; I checked [Arzhantsev–Petravchuk, Lemmas 4–5, p.5](https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0608157). Set `r=deg_y H`. Composition degrees and `deg F=deg_y F` imply `deg H=r`; attained positive `deg_y Q` implies `r|gcd(n,m,D₂)`, namely 11 or 9. Since the highest forms of F are `y²⁷(y−x)⁷²` and `y²⁴(y−x)⁸⁴`, unique factorization forces `(r,deg f)=(11,9)` and `(9,12)` respectively.
